The couples dance each week in a live show. The judges score each performance out of ten. After all the couples have danced they are then ranked according to the judges' scores and given points according to their rank, with the highest ranked couple receiving a number of points equal to the number of couples dancing that week e.g. 7 points where there are seven couples dancing. When there are no tied scores the lowest scored couple will receive one point. However in the event of a tie where two or more couples obtain the same judges score, the couple below those in the tie will be awarded one point below the points awarded to each of the tied couples. So, for example, if two couples obtain the same rank and obtain 7 points each, the couple immediately below them will be awarded 6 points. When couples are ranked equally by the judges the scoring of all other couples underneath will follow in the same descending order. Should there be any tied scores the lowest scored couple will therefore receive more than one point from the judges scores. The public are also invited to vote for their favourite couples, and the couples are ranked again according to the number of votes they receive, again receiving points; The couple with the most votes receiving the most points. Again in the unlikely  event of a tie in the public vote the points are awarded in the same way as the points from the judges score.

The points for judges' score and public vote are then added together, and the two couples with the fewest points are placed in the bottom two. If two couples have equal points, the points from the public vote are given precedence.<ref>{{Cite web |title=BBC One – Strictly Come Dancing – About |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/articles/16rGc8M34fT0wWYmrSMc8Cp/about |access-date=2024-12-01 |website=BBC |language=en-GB}}</ref>

As with the previous series, the bottom two couples have to perform a dance-off on the results show. Based on that performance alone, each judge then votes on which couple should stay and which couple should leave, with [[Shirley Ballas]], as head judge, having the last and [[Casting vote|deciding vote]], if needed.

== Professional dancers ==
In June 2024, the BBC announced that [[Dianne Buswell]], [[Nadiya Bychkova]], [[Vito Coppola]], [[Graziano Di Prima]], [[Amy Dowden]], [[Carlos Gu]], [[Karen Hauer]], [[Katya Jones]], [[Neil Jones (dancer)|Neil Jones]], [[Nikita Kuzmin]], [[Gorka Márquez]], [[Luba Mushtuk]], [[Lauren Oakley]], [[Jowita Przystał]], [[Johannes Radebe]], [[Michelle Tsiakkas]], [[Kai Widdrington]] and [[Nancy Xu]] would be returning to the series.<ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly Come Dancing confirms 2024 professionals |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-2024-professionals-newsupdate/ |website=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=14 July 2024}}</ref> It was confirmed that [[Giovanni Pernice]] would not be returning to the show, following misconduct allegations regarding his dance teaching methods.<ref name="auto">{{cite web |title=Strictly star Giovanni rejects claims over teaching methods |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-69034518 |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=8 July 2024 |date=19 May 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=BBC promises 'fairness' after Strictly Come Dancing complaint reports |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/clkk2dvrkgzo |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=14 July 2024 |language=en-gb |date=29 May 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title='It's not going to go away': Strictly Come Dancing row could take shine off 20th anniversary {{!}} Strictly Come Dancing {{!}} The Guardian |url=https://theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/article/2024/jul/13/strictly-come-dancing-row-could-take-shine-off-20th-anniversary |website=[[The Guardian]] |date=13 July 2024 |access-date=14 July 2024 |last1=Topping |first1=Alexandra }}</ref> Pernice, however, denied "any suggestion of abusive or threatening behaviour".<ref>{{cite web |title=Giovanni Pernice will not return to Strictly Come Dancing |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgeedq2zjjeo.amp |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=8 July 2024 |language=en-gb |date=10 June 2024}}</ref><ref name="auto"/> 

In July 2024, it was announced that [[Aljaž Škorjanec]] would be returning as a professional after a two-year hiatus, following his departure in March 2022, having last appeared in the [[Strictly Come Dancing series 19|nineteenth series]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Aljaž Škorjanec returns to the Strictly Come Dancing Ballroom as a Professional Dancer |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2024/aljaz-skorjanec-returns-to-strictly-come-dancing |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=14 July 2024 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Aljaž Škorjanec returns to Strictly Come Dancing |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c3g65wd9537o |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=14 July 2024 |language=en-gb |date=9 July 2024}}</ref> Later that same month, despite initially being confirmed to return for the series, it was subsequently announced that Graziano Di Prima would not be returning to the show, following allegations of misconduct against him towards [[Zara McDermott]], his partner from the [[Strictly Come Dancing series 21|previous series]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly star axed by BBC after 'deeply regretful' event |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/strictly-graziano-di-prima-zara-mcdermott-bbc-b2579463.html |website=[[The Independent]] |access-date=14 July 2024 |language=en |date=14 July 2024}}</ref> In a statement, Di Prima said that he "deeply regretted" the events that led to his departure from the show.<ref>{{cite web |title=Graziano Di Prima out of Strictly Come Dancing line-up |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c4ngl4qkjgeo |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=13 July 2024 |date=13 July 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly Come Dancing star Graziano Di Prima leaves BBC show |url=https://news.sky.com/story/strictly-come-dancing-star-graziano-di-prima-leaves-bbc-show-amid-reports-of-alleged-misconduct-13177469 |website=[[Sky News]] |access-date=14 July 2024 |language=en}}</ref>

During the launch show, Michelle Tsiakkas received a celebrity partner for the first time, while Carlos Gu, Lauren Oakley and Kai Widdrington did not receive a partner. The rest of the pros were paired to a celebrity, including Neil Jones, who did not have a celebrity partner for the last two series.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/mediacentre/2024/strictly-come-dancing-couples-revealed-launch-show|title=Strictly Come Dancing 2024 couples revealed in launch show featuring epic performances and Amy Dowden's momentous return to the ballroom|publisher=[[BBC]]|date=2024-09-14|access-date=2024-09-17|language=en-gb}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://uk.news.yahoo.com/strictly-disappointment-pros-snubbed-092907894.html?guccounter=1&guce_referrer=aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbS8&guce_referrer_sig=AQAAAAF_9R5YVwdHH06RO7A6Vvk_oo_FQSu0D9LqRw9lUZ0kf8fhANq_94w-3WLtEmRVRczf-dP2_TnMGwXJHg-f19XJP7Znb9K6zK1mHhQ_Mx0TCfh5f-mPzRQs_MrqSKZ_UbI6WbWRbg5Jnx7D925AXdK4D1rhlaroKK91YUJlISnu|title=Strictly disappointment as three pros snubbed and no same-sex couple|publisher=[[Yahoo]]|website=[[Yahoo News]]|first=Lily|last=Waddell|date=2024-09-16|access-date=2024-09-17|language=en-gb}}</ref>

On 4 November 2024, it was announced that due to a foot injury, Amy Dowden would no longer compete in the series. Oakley took over from Dowden as [[JB Gill]]'s professional partner.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c7741vn5myko|title=Amy Dowden will not return to Strictly this year|publisher=[[BBC]]|first=Noor|last=Nanji|date=4 November 2024|access-date=7 November 2024|language=en-gb}}</ref>

==Couples==
On 1 August 2024, prior to the official BBC announcements, [[Tom Dean (swimmer)|Tom Dean]] confirmed himself as the first participant in the series, during an interview at the [[2024 Summer Olympics]] after competing in the [[Swimming at the 2024 Summer Olympics – Men's 4 × 200 metre freestyle relay|4 × 200 metre freestyle relay]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly Come Dancing 2024: Olympic swimmer Tom Dean to join show |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cgr5rdjz7gvo |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=2 August 2024}}</ref> The official announcements began on 5 August, with [[Chris McCausland]] and [[JB Gill]] announced, the former becoming the first blind contestant to appear on the show.<ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly Come Dancing 2024: Chris McCausland and JB Gill announced as first two celebrity contestants |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c39kklz2nzxo |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=5 August 2024 |language=en-gb |date=5 August 2024}}</ref> Celebrity contestants continued to be revealed until 12 August 2024, when the full line-up was announced.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.express.co.uk/showbiz/tv-radio/1935197/strictly-come-dancing-final-3-celebrities-line-up|title=Strictly Come Dancing confirm final 3 celebrity contestants – completing 2024 line-up|work=[[Daily Express]]|first=Hayley|last=Anderson|date=12 August 2024|access-date=12 August 2024|language=en-gb}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.standard.co.uk/showbiz/celebrity-news/bbc-one-diy-sos-actor-gladiators-adam-peaty-b1176142.html|title=Strictly Come Dancing 2024 contestants: Full line-up revealed|work=[[Evening Standard]]|first=Charlotte|last=McLaughlin|date=12 August 2024|access-date=12 August 2024|language=en-gb}}</ref>
